    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0584" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.154/231a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Dwight D.
                            Eisenhower
                    </hi><anchor n="9" xml:id="d538-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-02">April 2, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: During a recent
                    conversation which I had with Ambassador Boal and Mr. Bonsal,<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d538-f2"/> of your Department, I was requested by the latter to
                    forward to you the War Department’s opinion as to the desirability, from a
                    military point of view, of building the Rama Road in Nicaragua.</p>
                <p>The subject of munitions of war under lend-lease for Nicaragua and certain other
                    military questions were also discussed.</p>
                <p>With respect to the building of the Rama Road, it is the opinion of the
                    Operations Section that the execution of this project will tend to increase the
                    stability of the country, and so minimize the possibility of trouble with
                    disaffected elements. The road would have a decided tactical value, should it
                    become necessary for United States troops to intervene, either because of
                    attempted uprising by the enemy nationals along the western coast, or because of
                    an attempted hostile raid.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dwight D. Eisenhower</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d538-f1" n="9" type="source" xml:id="d538-f1-content">
                <p>General Eisenhower was Assistant Chief of Staff, Operations Division, War
                    Department General Staff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d538-f2" n="10" xml:id="d538-f2-content">
                <p>Pierre de L. Boal, Ambassador to Nicaragua, and Philip W. Bonsal, Chief of the
                    Division of the American Republics.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
